# Commits (Aron-Chu)

## Author (every commit)

All commits must be **solely attributed to Aron-Chu**:

```
Aron-Chu <aroncloudchu@gmail.com>
```

- **Do not** add `Co-authored-by:` trailers (Cursor, agents, bots).
- **Do not** change `user.name` / `user.email` in git config unless the user asks.
- When committing on behalf of the user, use env vars for this commit only:

```powershell
$env:GIT_AUTHOR_NAME = 'Aron-Chu'
$env:GIT_AUTHOR_EMAIL = 'aroncloudchu@gmail.com'
$env:GIT_COMMITTER_NAME = 'Aron-Chu'
$env:GIT_COMMITTER_EMAIL = 'aroncloudchu@gmail.com'
```

**Cursor may auto-append** `Co-authored-by: Cursor` on agent commits. If that happens, rewrite the message with `git commit-tree` + `git update-ref refs/heads/master <new>` (message file with no trailer), or commit yourself in a terminal outside the agent.

## Message format

Follow [Conventional Commits](https://www.conventionalcommits.org/) — see `CONTRIBUTING.md`.

```
type(scope): short imperative summary

Optional body explaining why (no Co-authored-by lines).
```

Examples: `feat(video): add VOD relay start API`, `fix(ci): do not block release on scraper checkout`.

## When to commit

- Only when the user explicitly asks to commit.
- Run pre-commit hooks; fix failures with a **new** commit (do not amend unless user rules allow).
- Never commit secrets (`.env`, tokens, `oauth-bundle.env`).

## Release tags

`VERSION` file and git tag (e.g. `v0.2.9`) must match before tagging. Pushing a tag triggers `release-images.yml` (GHCR + Setup.exe).
